# Expected code blocks for troubleshooting_slow_requests, the whole page (../../headings/published/troubleshooting_slow_requests.html)
# Format: checks/codeblocks.py. Written with codeblocks.py --emit from the
# published page, then edited by hand: types are the native mode's (see
# the page's intent .md);
# block 4 is the source's whole block, which the published page breaks
# into paragraphs after its first line.
=== type=bash place=body | Experiment 1: Measure total round-trip app requests
time curl -v APP-ENDPOINT
=== type=console place=body | Experiment 1: Measure total round-trip app requests
$ time curl -v http://app1.app_domain.com

GET /hello HTTP/1.1
Host: app1.app_domain.com
User-Agent: curl/7.43.0
Accept: */*

HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json;charset=utf-8
Date: Tue, 14 Dec 2019 00:31:32 GMT
Server: nginx
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
X-Vcap-Request-Id: c30fad28-4972-46eb-7da6-9d07dc79b109
Content-Length: 602
hello world!

real 2m0.707s
user 0m0.005s
sys  0m0.007s
=== type=bash place=list | Experiment 2: View request time in access logs
cf logs APP-NAME
=== type=console place=list | Experiment 2: View request time in access logs
$ cf logs app1

2019-12-14T00:33:32.35-0800 [RTR/0] OUT app1.app_domain.com - [14/12/2019:00:31:32.348 +0000] "GET /hello HTTP/1.1" 200 0 60 "-" "HTTPClient/1.0 (2.7.1, ruby 2.3.3 (2019-11-21))" "10.0.4.207:20810" "10.0.48.67:61555" x_forwarded_for:"52.3.107.171" x_forwarded_proto:"http" vcap_request_id:"01144146-1e7a-4c77-77ab-49ae3e286fe9" response_time:120.00641734 gorouter_time:0.000217 app_id:"13ee085e-bdf5-4a48-aaaf-e854a8a975df" app_index:"0" x_b3_traceid:"3595985e7c34536a" x_b3_spanid:"3595985e7c34536a" x_b3_parentspanid:"-"
2019-12-14T00:32:32.35-0800 [APP/PROC/WEB/0]OUT app1 received request at [14/12/2019:00:32:32.348 +0000] with "vcap_request_id": "01144146-1e7a-4c77-77ab-49ae3e286fe9"
^C
=== type=bash place=list | Experiment 3: Duplicate latency on another endpoint
time curl -v TEST-APP-ENDPOINT
=== type=bash place=list | Experiment 4: Remove the load balancer from request path
bosh ssh router/ROUTER-GUID
=== type=bash place=list | Experiment 4: Remove the load balancer from request path
time curl ROUTER-IP -H "Host: TEST-APP-ENDPOINT"
=== type=bash place=list | Experiment 5: Remove Gorouter from request path
cf ssh TEST-APP -c "env | grep CF_INSTANCE_ADDR"
=== type=console place=list | Experiment 5: Remove Gorouter from request path
$ cf ssh my-app -c "env | grep CF_INSTANCE_ADDR"
=== type=bash place=list | Experiment 5: Remove Gorouter from request path
bosh ssh router/ROUTER-GUID
